BT /F1 9.7 Tf 47 702.00 Td (40 MCQs | 60 minutes | One best answer \(A-D\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 47 679.00 Td (Name: __________________________   Index: __________________________) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 651.00 Td (01. A patient has a sudden rise in arteriolar sympathetic firing with minimal change in) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 636.30 Td (cardiac output. Which immediate variable rises most directly?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 617.60 Td (A. The intrinsic rate of the SA node.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 602.90 Td (B. The rate of tissue metabolite clearance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 588.20 Td (C. Total peripheral resistance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 573.50 Td (D. Systemic venous compliance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 547.80 Td (02. The R-R separation is four large squares on a regular standard-speed ECG. What is) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 533.10 Td (the heart rate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 514.40 Td (A. 75 beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 499.70 Td (B. 120 beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 485.00 Td (C. 60 beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 470.30 Td (D. 90 beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 444.60 Td (03. Portal hypertension promotes ascites partly by increasing which force?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 425.90 Td (A. Plasma oncotic pressure within hepatic capillaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 411.20 Td (B. Hydrostatic pressure in hepatic sinusoids.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 396.50 Td (C. Interstitial lymphatic pumping efficiency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 381.80 Td (D. Arterial oxygen tension in the hepatic vein.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 356.10 Td (04. Which contrast best distinguishes forward failure from backward failure?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 337.40 Td (A. Forward reduces delivery; backward causes venous congestion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 322.70 Td (B. Forward is venous congestion; backward is low organ blood flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 308.00 Td (C. Forward indicates excess cardiac output; backward low afterload.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 293.30 Td (D. Forward is confined to the right heart; backward to the left.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 267.60 Td (05. What directly promotes pulmonary oedema in left-sided backward heart failure?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 248.90 Td (A. Reduced pulmonary capillary hydrostatic pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 234.20 Td (B. Reduced systemic venous pressure throughout the body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 219.50 Td (C. Raised pulmonary venous and capillary pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 204.80 Td (D. Raised right atrial pressure without lung congestion.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 179.10 Td (06. Why does the fetal cardiovascular system divert much blood away from the pulmonary) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 164.40 Td (circuit before birth?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 145.70 Td (A. The fetal left ventricle cannot generate arterial pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 131.00 Td (B. Pulmonary vascular resistance is exceptionally low before birth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 116.30 Td (C. Umbilical arteries carry already oxygenated blood to the heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 101.60 Td (D. The placenta oxygenates blood; fetal lungs resist flow.) Tj ET
