BT /F1 7.2 Tf 47 814 Td (DOMiNANCE CVS | MOCK 04) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 748.00 Td (07. An ECG electrode detects a voltage on the skin even though the impulse originates) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 733.30 Td (in the myocardium. What makes this possible?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 714.60 Td (A. The heart mechanically transmits its pulse to every skin electrode.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 699.90 Td (B. The electrodes measure changes in circulating blood pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 685.20 Td (C. Cardiac electrical currents spread through conducting body tissues.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 670.50 Td (D. The chest electrodes directly contact ventricular muscle fibres.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 644.80 Td (08. Heart rate rises from 70 to 80 beats/min while stroke volume stays at 70 mL. By how) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 630.10 Td (much does cardiac output increase?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 611.40 Td (A. By 0.80 litres per minute.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 596.70 Td (B. By 0.70 litres per minute.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 582.00 Td (C. By about 0.49 litres per minute.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 567.30 Td (D. By 1.40 litres per minute.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 541.60 Td (09. Most sympathetic constrictor fibres release noradrenaline onto arteriolar smooth) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 526.90 Td (muscle. Which receptor mainly mediates constriction?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 508.20 Td (A. The beta-2 adrenergic receptor on vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 493.50 Td (B. The muscarinic M2 receptor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 478.80 Td (C. The endothelial H2 receptor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 464.10 Td (D. The alpha-1 adrenergic receptor.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 438.40 Td (10. A harsh systolic murmur develops during blood ejection through a narrowed aortic) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 423.70 Td (valve. What mechanism explains it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 405.00 Td (A. Opening of the aortic valve during ventricular relaxation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 390.30 Td (B. Turbulent forward flow through a stenotic outflow orifice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 375.60 Td (C. Regurgitation through the mitral valve during diastole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 360.90 Td (D. Laminar blood flow through a normal-sized valve.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 335.20 Td (11. At 25 mm/s, a PR interval extends across 4.5 small squares. Which interpretation is) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 320.50 Td (most accurate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 301.80 Td (A. 0.24 s, above the stated PR-interval range.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 287.10 Td (B. 0.09 s, shorter than the stated normal PR-interval range.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 272.40 Td (C. 0.90 s, above the stated PR-interval range.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 257.70 Td (D. 0.18 s, inside the stated PR-interval range.) Tj ET
