BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 748.00 Td (13. During severe hepatic hypoperfusion, cells near the central vein are especially) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 733.30 Td (vulnerable to hypoxia. Why?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 714.60 Td (A. They are located outside the hepatic sinusoidal network.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 699.90 Td (B. They are closest to arterial inflow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 685.20 Td (C. They are farthest downstream from the portal triads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 670.50 Td (D. They receive blood with the highest oxygen content.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 644.80 Td (14. Following a substantial meal, intestinal blood flow rises for several hours. What) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 630.10 Td (primarily drives this response?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 611.40 Td (A. Global sympathetic constriction of intestinal arteries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 596.70 Td (B. Reduced intestinal metabolism during nutrient absorption.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 582.00 Td (C. Complete diversion of portal blood away from liver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 567.30 Td (D. Local metabolic activity and absorptive demand.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 541.60 Td (15. Two Frank-Starling curves are plotted against identical end-diastolic volumes. What) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 526.90 Td (does an upward shift of the entire curve usually indicate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 508.20 Td (A. Greater contractility at the same preload.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 493.50 Td (B. Greater afterload alone with unchanged contractility.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 478.80 Td (C. Aortic valve closure earlier in systole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 464.10 Td (D. Lower force development at every fibre length.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 438.40 Td (16. During a stress response, circulating adrenaline dilates vessels in working) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 423.70 Td (skeletal muscle while constricting many skin vessels. Why?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 405.00 Td (A. The muscle vessels lack any adrenergic receptors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 390.30 Td (B. Different vascular beds express different adrenergic receptors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 375.60 Td (C. Skin tissue receives a much lower concentration of adrenaline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 360.90 Td (D. Different vascular beds contain markedly different amounts of plasma.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 335.20 Td (17. In severe haemorrhagic shock, why does sympathetic constriction of splanchnic) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 320.50 Td (vessels help initially?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 301.80 Td (A. It increases flow to the intestinal mucosa above baseline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 287.10 Td (B. It increases hepatic oxygen extraction to 100%.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 272.40 Td (C. It prevents all intestinal ischaemia during shock.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 257.70 Td (D. It redistributes flow and mobilises stored venous blood.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 232.00 Td (18. An examination reveals raised JVP, a tender enlarged liver, ascites and ankle) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 217.30 Td (oedema. Which haemodynamic change unifies these?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 198.60 Td (A. High systemic venous pressure behind the right ventricle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 183.90 Td (B. Reduced filtration from peripheral capillaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 169.20 Td (C. Increased pulmonary venous pressure without systemic congestion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 154.50 Td (D. Reduced central venous pressure from depleted blood volume.) Tj ET
